\label{rem:k-dependence}
The intrinsic dimension enters through the minima-selection subproblem, most visibly via the \(N^{-1/\texttt{k}}\) approximation term in \Cref{thm:main-et2-bound}.
This matches the worst-case intuition that optimizing over a \(\texttt{k}\)-dimensional nonconvex minimizer manifold can reduce to \(\texttt{k}\)-dimensional global optimization and exhibit \(\Omega(\varepsilon^{-\texttt{k}})\)-type hardness \citep[Rem.~1.1]{masiha2025superquantile}.

